{"title":"South Korean aspirational markets in everything","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/968783027/0/marginalrevolution~South-Korean-aspirational-markets-in-everything.html","date":1788806480000,"content":"<blockquote>\r\n<p>Instead of Amazon, I spent the past week browsing a new breed of websites known as “dopamine sites,” a trend that emerged in South Korea. These websites — like <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://dopamineshop.co/\" target=\"_blank\">Dopamine Shop</a> and <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://foodnevercomes.com/#menu\" target=\"_blank\">FoodNeverComes</a> — recreate the entire ritual of online shopping: You search for products, compare reviews, add items to your cart, enter a shipping address, place an order, and even track your delivery.</p>\r\n<p>Then … nothing happens. No money changes hands. No package arrives.</p>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n<p>Here is <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://restofworld.org/2026/south-korea-shopping-trend/\" target=\"_blank\">more from Itika Sharma Punit</a>.  Via the excellent <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://x.com/samirvarma\" target=\"_blank\">Samir Varma</a>.</p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/09/south-korean-aspirational-markets-in-everything.html\">South Korean aspirational markets in everything</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/968783027/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/968783027/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/968783